  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer infrared bandpass filter on CaF2 substrate with alternating Ge and ZnS layers (Ge first, ZnS second, repeating for 24 total layers). Wavelength bands: passbands at 4150-4350 nm and 4550-4750 nm, stopbands at 3600-4000 nm and 4850-5200 nm. Normal incidence, unpolarized light, coherent TMM. Initialize all layer thicknesses to 550 nm for Ge and 900 nm for ZnS (quarter-wave at ~4500 nm). Optimization bounds: 200-1500 nm for all layers. Use differential_evolution_thickness optimizer with population size 50, max generations 200. Objective: maximize weighted sum of mean transmittance in both passbands minus mean transmittance in both stopbands. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 3600-4000 nm, 4150-4350 nm, 4550-4750 nm, 4850-5200 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 4.15-4.35 um and 4.55-4.75 um bands; low transmittance in 3.60-4.00 um and 4.85-5.20 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance in stopbands; high reflectance in passbands. manufacturing constraints: no metal layers; maximum 24 layers; conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a 24-layer coherent dielectric bandpass filter on CaF2 with alternating Ge and ZnS layers. Maximize mean transmittance in 4150-4350 nm and 4550-4750 nm passbands while minimizing mean transmittance in 3600-4000 nm and 4850-5200 nm stopbands at normal incidence. Layer thicknesses bounded between 200 and 1500 nm.",
